{"id": "EUVD-2026-82240", "enisaUuid": "331c4bee-6b94-3317-b242-4e9e278e8802", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: RISC-V: Fix riscv_acpi_add_prt_dep() loop handling\n\nThe loop in riscv_acpi_add_prt_dep() includes error conditions that are\nhandled in a dubious - if not outright wrong - way, by continuining the\nloop (which skips and misses the entry pointer update to point to the next\nentry).\n\nRewrite the loop as a for loop (that handles the continuation correctly)\nand wrap the condition and update statements using helper functions to make\nit cleaner.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:06:05", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/41652ca8c6ff2b77b9780cbbb2f20f1551b9ff80", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c9729ced165d6c5b57d99141b6632bb8711efec9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3fd86a5d6facb6618f63a76d499f28007cef878f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a56321d0aceee2a0bd80d23366401c131ff8350"], "aliases": ["GHSA-w98f-qgf3-22gf", "CVE-2026-93132"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "48c50a4c-553f-385b-a78d-314b6f104ce6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "60d9c006-1e2f-3671-af42-5dafe37776d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1b173cc4bfcdcf4a49927952ba3a445c5b293723 <3a56321d0aceee2a0bd80d23366401c131ff8350"}, {"id": "6c9cd28c-c5ca-33d4-8517-5a92f753240e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "82f2e65c-a244-336f-8e10-254ad4a7cdb7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "8c839818-effc-3363-8156-883657e7fc51", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1b173cc4bfcdcf4a49927952ba3a445c5b293723 <c9729ced165d6c5b57d99141b6632bb8711efec9"}, {"id"